source_note:
**Sources.** Data: [U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Unemployment Rate (`UNRATE`)](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/UNRATE), via FRED;
Japan: [OECD, Infra-annual labour statistics, unemployment rate (`LRHUTTTTJPA156S`)](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/LRHUTTTTJPA156S), via FRED;
Europe (the euro area of 12) and 40 other countries: [European Commission, AMECO database, unemployment rate (`ZUTN`)](https://economy-finance.ec.europa.eu/economic-research-and-databases/economic-databases/ameco-database_en);
other OECD and G20 members: [International Labour Organization modelled estimates, Unemployment, total (`SL.UEM.TOTL.ZS`)](https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/SL.UEM.TOTL.ZS),
via the World Bank's World Development Indicators. Country groups: [World Bank country classifications](https://datahelpdesk.worldbank.org/knowledgebase/articles/906519-world-bank-country-and-lending-groups).
Prepared files: [`data/ch01/fig1-4.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch01/fig1-4.csv), [`data/ch01/unemployment_world.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch01/unemployment_world.csv) and [`data/ch01/countries.csv`](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch01/countries.csv)
(see the [data notes](https://github.com/quarcs-lab/macro102-site/blob/main/data/ch01/README.md)).
Chart: inspired by Fig. 1.4 in Jones (2024), [*Macroeconomics*, 6th ed.](https://wwnorton.com/books/9781324063612)
